From d31837453e3e90004e4ed40e03225b65310f46cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:24:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] REACH wired: the S2B terrain is now consumed and coverage is
 reported per direction. Root cause of both prior failures found by reading
 the enclosing function: the REACH block sits inside s3b_family_evidence, not
 a separate S5B function, and ent_map was never defined there; cp.book_events
 already returns {1: long entry bars, -1: short entry bars}, which is exactly
 the shape coverage_by_direction wants, so the fix is to bind ev_book. Three
 further latent NameErrors in the same scope fixed: segment_label was
 referenced but never assigned, selection was not imported, and s5b_selection
 was called by the --stage S5B dispatch but did not exist. The denominator is
 the S2B terrain built by terrain.build_terrain, the same construction and
 grid S2B writes, never a locally improvised episode set. Coverage is never
 pooled: the BOTH row is labelled reported-only and is not the score.
 entry_pos_median is emitted as a descriptive column because coverage counts
 presence, not capture, and no taper is built on it.

---
 dot_master_discovery/engine/selection.py | 13 ++++++++++-
 dot_master_discovery/master.py           | 28 ++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dot_master_discovery/engine/selection.py b/dot_master_discovery/engine/selection.py
